WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:13.180
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:13.180
TAKARA FANSUBS

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.830
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.580
Overlooking the rows of houses and stores

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.280
from the highest vantage,

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:26.780
Such things as tears and sadness

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.680
will quickly vanish

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.880
The birds, wind, and sunshine...

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.880
...all are your friends

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:45.790
I'll carry this dream farther than far

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:50.390
...no matter the distance...

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:57.590
I long to fly freely

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:01.790
through the blue sky in my heart...

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.690
The far distant blue sky

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:12.190
It flows into tomorrow

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:32.980
The only way fro Romeo to save his father's life

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:37.580
was for Romeo to become a chimney sweep.

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.180
Romeo came to his decision.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:44.680
With his family watching,

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.380
Romeo boarded the carriage of the God of Death

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.580
and started his journey to Milan.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:58.180
Episode 4:

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:58.180
The Boy on the Poster

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.580
Ummm...

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.180
By what means are we travelling to Milan?

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:47.580
Get off.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:50.180
I said GET OFF!

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:55.880
Head straight and you'll reach Locarno.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.180
Make your way to a shop called "The Wildcat" by nightfall.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:07.080
I'll get there after I've settled some business.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:08.280
Wait! But...

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:13.380
And... if you are thinking of escape, keep in mind that I wouldn't let you live.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.680
Got it? "The Wildcat."

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.430
No way...

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:07.280
Piccolo!

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.180
Why you! When did you manage to sneak aboard?

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:19.380
You want to come along too?

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:22.580
Hey! Stop that! That tickles!

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.280
What a rascal you are...

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.680
We're not going there just to play, you know!

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.780
But I can't just leave you here...

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:32.280
So what should I...

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:35.980
Will you be good, and not cause any trouble?

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.580
In that case, I'll take you along.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:40.930
We'll start out when the rain stops.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:44.780
Let's eat lunch while we're waiting.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:49.480
Here.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.280
Thanks to you, I'm feeling lots better!

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:00.680
No fair, Piccolo!

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.280
That's mine!

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:25.780
Barchelo!

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:28.580
Barchelo!

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:39.480
Hey! Caught you in the act, you little apple thief!

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:42.380
Thief? I just now picked this up off the ground.

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.480
Shuddup! C'mon over here.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:48.380
What?! Half of the apples are gone.

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.580
Where'd you put the other apples?

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.530
I didn't steal ANYTHING.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:53.380
Don't lie!

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.180
I'm NOT lying!

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.380
What's all this fuss now?

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:57.580
Seems to be a thief.

00:05:58.180 --> 00:05:59.180
You're mistaken... I'm

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:00.380
SHADDUP!

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.480
I was just walking by!

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:04.880
Can it, I'm calling the police.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:09.580
- Please! Just listen to me!
- Will you stand still! And shut up! Damn!

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.780
Hey, Antonio, why not listen to what he's got to say?

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:14.680
"Got to say"...?!

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:18.180
It's simple... I packed these apples in Locarno,

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:20.280
a pile of apples as high as the Alps...

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.780
and now this is all that's left in the basket!

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:25.980
That brat stole them, and is just trying to get out of it!

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:28.880
You probably sneaked under that tarp...

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:31.280
and were eating to your heart's content!

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:33.180
So that's it!

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:35.580
You've been hiding there since Locarno, haven't you?

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:36.680
You're wrong!

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:40.480
I've been walking for hours -- from Sonogno village!

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:43.280
I was about to GO to Locarno!

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.880
Shaddup! Come on, I'm taking you to the police!

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:47.380
Wait!

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:49.280
That boy is innocent.

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:51.880
And I'll show you the proof.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:55.080
His shoes are muddy.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:59.280
This is clear evidence of his walking for hours in the rain.

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:02.780
If he had been hiding under that tarp,

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.380
his shoes wouldn't be so filthy.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:05.780
That makes a lot of sense!

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:07.280
That's true, isn't it!

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:10.080
Better give up while you're ahead, Antonio.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.080
And anyways, mister...

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:14.880
it's thirty minutes to ride here from Locarno.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:16.680
In just thirty minutes

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:19.780
could someone eat a pile of apples that was as high as the Alps?

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:21.580
That's tight!

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:23.380
I couldn't have eaten them!

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:24.580
Couldn't have eaten them!

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.580
So, where did my apples go?

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.780
There you are.
It seems we've caught our apple thief!

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.080
Barchelo!

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.880
You did all this! You're gonna get it!

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:42.080
Barchelo!

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:43.180
I'm sorry, Dad!

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:44.680
I'll give you "sorry"!!

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:45.580
Forgive me!

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.380
Hold it, you!

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:51.580
Do this again, and I'll REALLY let you have it!

00:07:58.480 --> 00:07:59.980
Sorry about this, son.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.080
That kid, he's unbelievable, stealing apples

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:06.380
and then hiding like that...

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.170
Say there!

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:11.680
Hold on!

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:13.980
Thanks for the help, just now.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:16.680
I'd have been in big trouble if you hadn't been here.

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:19.080
You're pretty smart. I'm impressed.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:21.280
It's no big deal.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.580
Here -- he gave these as an apology.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.380
Have one.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:29.230
Ok, thanks.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:31.780
I'm Romeo. And you?

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:51.230
The market opens today in Locarno.

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:55.080
You can read? That's great!

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:57.580
In my village, the only ones who can read

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.780
are the priest and... uh...

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.480
Hey, wait!

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:14.630
Isn't this you?

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:34.980
What a pretty girl!

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:38.880
I've got a friend like her called Anita.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:58.880
Hey!

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:08.680
Wow!

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:10.680
You're a fast walker, aren't you?

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:12.880
You have some business with me?

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:16.680
These are really delicious apples!

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:18.780
Eat some, and you'll feel better.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:20.780
And that was why...

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.380
you went to the trouble of running after me?

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:23.780
Don't you want it?

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:34.280
Thank you.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:36.630
That's better!

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:39.480
Sort of a strange guy, aren't you?

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:41.080
You think so?

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.580
You said you were going to Locarno?

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:44.380
Yes.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:45.580
Come on.

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:56.780
That's Locarno!

00:10:57.780 --> 00:11:01.630
Wow! What a huge town!

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:03.580
What's that lake?

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:04.930
That's the Lago Maggiore.

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:16.280
I wonder if I'll be able to find this "Wildcat" shop...

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:18.080
"Wildcat"?

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:20.080
I've got to go there.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:22.380
You wouldn't be going to Milan, would you?

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:24.030
Th... That's right!

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:25.880
To become a chimney sweep?

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:27.930
How did you know that?

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:30.080
I'm doing the same.

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:33.180
You're going to become a chimney sweep too?

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:08.480
Today's big bargain is this corn!

00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:10.280
Come on over, come one over! Let's deal!

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:14.080
The latest fashion in shoes! Just imported from Milan!

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:18.330
Newspaper! Newspaper! The Geneva murder!

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:21.080
And look, the culprit turned out to be Baiorishti!

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:25.880
Newspaper! Newspaper! Just off the Locarno Gazette!

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:30.880
This is the first time I've seen so many shops at once!

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:33.780
Locarno is the biggest town in the area.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:37.280
And its marketplace is also famous for being really lively.

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:42.680
I'm going to have a little look!

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:48.780
It was Romeo's first sight of most of the goods

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:52.080
which were being sold in the marketplace.

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:55.680
Alfredo was kind enough to explain

00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:58.430
many new things to Romeo.

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:07.380
What's this? It's different from the other dolls.

00:13:07.480 --> 00:13:09.080
It's a music box.

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:10.280
A music box?

00:13:10.280 --> 00:13:12.130
Yes. Let me see it.

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:26.630
I once saw a music box like this in Lugano.

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:28.880
You've been to Lugano?

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:29.680
Yes.

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:32.980
You know about so many things!

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:35.130
You must have been raised in a wonderful family.

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:38.480
But why are you becoming a chimney sweep?

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:50.680
Understand this, Romeo.

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:52.580
My name is Alfredo.

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:54.380
I don't want to say anything more.

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:58.930
Be careful!

00:13:58.980 --> 00:13:59.980
Sorry!

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:01.880
Would anyone like a newspaper?

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:04.580
Wait!

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:09.180
I understand!

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:10.580
I won't ask you anything more.

00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:15.080
I promise, Alfredo.

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:18.180
Agreed, Romeo.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:19.480
All right! Let's go!

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:20.380
Ok!

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:24.480
What's wrong, Dad?

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:27.080
Did you see something that would make a good article?

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:30.080
The boy who just passed looks exactly like the kid in this picture.

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:31.280
Let's see...

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:32.480
"Missing person."

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:36.590
"Fifty francs reward for information regarding these two siblings...

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:42.380
"..and one hundred francs reward for their return."

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:43.680
A HUNDRED FRANCS?!

00:14:44.180 --> 00:14:45.780
Who on earth ARE these kids?

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:47.280
I don't know.

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:48.880
One moment, I'll check it out...

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:54.780
I wonder what that is?

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:55.380
Let's go see.

00:14:55.380 --> 00:14:56.180
Right!

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:09.580
Lost them.

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:14.980
And now, everyone, the greatest acrobat in all of Locarno --

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:16.880
Michelangelo!

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:30.430
I can't see...

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:32.080
What are they doing?

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:36.680
Ah! It's a bear!
And he's walking on a barrel!

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:38.780
STOP!

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:39.580
What's wrong?

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:41.180
Someone stole my bag!

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:43.780
Move it! Move it!

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:50.480
He's gone! Where is he?

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:52.080
There's an alley back there.

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:53.680
That must be it!

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:02.780
Someone chasing you?

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:04.480
Who the hell are you?

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:07.180
Split it half-and-half with me and I'll save you.

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:08.380
Say what?

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:11.980
I'm offering you an escape route, ya know.

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:13.880
Why you... I wouldn't give you...

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:15.980
Hey! Thief!

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:18.780
All right! All right! I'll give you half!

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:25.380
What a jerk!

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:26.780
No more than you are.

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:29.280
Now, my share, please.

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:31.380
Here's your share!

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:34.380
God-DAMMIT!

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:37.480
That guy's gonna get it!

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:50.980
You asshole!

00:16:52.580 --> 00:16:53.580
Shit!

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:55.480
I'll take that, thanks!

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:56.780
That's MY bag.

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:07.380
I appreciate your help back there.

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:08.480
Thanks.

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:12.280
Allright, allright, I'll give it back.

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:13.680
Watch out!

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:18.980
Ya damn sneak!

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:23.780
Sunk your bag, didn't he...

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:48.280
Romeo, you're not gonna...?

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:50.480
Sure am!

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:03.380
Faster! Faster! What're you doing, you dolt?

00:18:13.180 --> 00:18:14.380
Just a little more!

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:15.180
Romeo!

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:16.580
Keep it up!

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:40.180
Romeo! Are you ok?

00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:42.580
I'm fine!
I'll find it for sure!

00:18:58.180 --> 00:18:59.880
Romeo! Forget it!

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:04.680
Thanks! But just forget it, Romeo!

00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:07.380
Found it!

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:08.880
Romeo!

00:19:08.980 --> 00:19:10.580
Alfredo... I found it!

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:15.680
Jeez, what a troublemaker!

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:17.980
Whoops... better get going!

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:26.680
Romeo...
I'm really grateful.

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:29.780
It's nothing... that time with the apples,

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:31.580
you helped me out then.

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:34.980
In this bag

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:37.680
is something more important than my life.

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:40.280
Something more important than your life...?

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:44.780
I won't forget what you've done today.

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:49.280
If something ever happens to you, I'll be the one to help you out.

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:08.880
You worthless brats.

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:12.680
What the hell are you doing screwing around till this late at night?

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:18.680
It... it took a long time to find this place...

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:20.380
Shut your face!

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:23.380
Romeo!

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:25.380
Stand up!

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:26.580
Come here.

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:43.180
Get in.

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:47.680
You guys are the last ones.

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:48.780
The last...?

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:49.980
Move!

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:51.480
Romeo!

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.380
Get over there and keep quiet.

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:06.780
Someone's there!

00:21:22.280 --> 00:21:24.780
Well, there's a familiar face...

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:25.880
Who are you?!

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:29.680
Hey now!
Forgotten me, have you?

00:21:34.080 --> 00:21:35.480
You!

00:21:56.580 --> 00:22:00.380
The boy I met in the tavern intends to escape!

00:22:00.580 --> 00:22:04.180
Alfredo says he wants to stay behind alone to keep from arousing suspicion to our plan...

00:22:04.280 --> 00:22:07.980
But I can't just leave you. We're friends, right?

00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:11.780
Next time:
A Night in the Tavern
See you then!

00:22:12.820 --> 00:22:16.820
"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"

00:22:25.920 --> 00:22:30.020
Si Si Ciao, why do the good times

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:34.320
seem to end so soon?

00:22:34.520 --> 00:22:38.520
Si Si Ciao, we're all friends

00:22:38.720 --> 00:22:42.720
Let's meet again on these Roman roofs

00:22:43.330 --> 00:22:47.630
Your laughing voice dances

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:51.530
Once again in the sky

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:58.830
Your pocket bursting with memories

00:23:00.530 --> 00:23:04.430
Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now

00:23:04.630 --> 00:23:08.630
Let's meet again on these Roman roofs
